GELLS-DEM V1.4: Full 3D Volumetric Simulation
Context
GELLS-DEM V1.3 is a 2D overdamped particle dynamics simulator with superellipse granule shapes. The primary goal of V1.4 is to upgrade to a full 3D volumetric simulation to model compaction, percolation, and transport through granular hydrogel scaffolds. This enables physically meaningful predictions of void-space evolution, permeability (Darcy/Kozeny-Carman), and phase connectivity that cannot be captured in 2D.

Key Decisions (from user input)
Single file: All simulation physics stays in new_dem_0.py (~3000+ lines)
3D rendering: PyVista primary when available, matplotlib fallback
Three modes: "2D" (pure V1.3), "2D-slice" (generate 3D, slice at midplane), "3D" (full volumetric)
Scale target: 500-1000 granules -- needs vectorized contact detection and Numba JIT for Newton-Raphson solver
