r_bound = max(a, b, c) in 3D
Phase 2: 3D Packing and Contact Detection
2a. generate_packing_3d()
3D random sequential addition in Lx x Ly x Lz box
Superellipsoid volume = (4/3) pi * r_eq^3 for equivalent radius
Scale semi-axes (a,b,c) to match target volume
Random quaternion orientation
Bounding-sphere overlap check for placement
2b. find_contact_superellipsoids() - 3D common normal method
Newton-Raphson with 4 unknowns (eta_i, omega_i, eta_j, omega_j)
Sphere fast-path when is_circle=True
Returns (in_contact, delta, nx, ny, nz, cx, cy, cz, R_eff)
2c. find_contact_superellipsoid_wall_3d() - 6 wall faces
Phase 3: 3D Forces and Integration
3a. Extend compute_forces()
Force array: (N,3) in 3D, (N,2) in 2D
