Phase 5: 2D-Slice Mode (mode="2D-slice")
Explicit third mode: "2D" = pure V1.3, "2D-slice" = generate 3D then slice, "3D" = full volumetric.

slice_superellipsoid_z() - Slice 3D superellipsoid at z-midplane to get 2D cross-section:

Transform z-plane to body frame via quaternion
Compute z-term: |z_body/c|^n2
Cross-section semi-axes: a_2d = a * (1-z_term)^(1/n2), same for b
Cross-section blockiness: n_2d = n1 (equatorial preserved)
Projected orientation from quaternion
Workflow: generate 3D packing -> slice at z=Lz/2 -> create 2D GranuleSystem -> run 2D simulation

