Phase 7b: Performance for 500-1000 Granules
Vectorized contact detection: Batch all candidate pairs from cKDTree, compute bounding-sphere overlaps as NumPy array operations before entering per-pair Newton-Raphson
Numba JIT: Decorate find_contact_superellipsoids() and superellipsoid_point/normal with @numba.njit for ~10-50x speedup on the inner Newton-Raphson loop
Bounding-box clipping in render_fields_3d(): Only evaluate implicit function within r_bound of each granule center
Optional Numba: Import with try/except, fall back to pure NumPy if unavailable. Add use_numba: bool = True to Params
Coarser 3D grid: Default Ngrid_3d=80 (512K voxels) is fine; user can lower to 50 for large runs
